{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"3c9ec47553a8191f938e934b684a0a38873f2ec2904fbf31fb96f0235f7f573e","occurred_at":"2026-11-21T21:11:45Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[222,223]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","quoted_text":"        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=qcow2\" % (run / \"overlay.qcow2\"),\n        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=raw,readonly=on\" % (run / \"seed.iso\"),","reason":"The current qemu_command interpolates the resolved run path directly into comma-delimited QEMU -drive option strings. It neither doubles embedded commas nor rejects comma-containing paths, so a path such as /tmp/probe,local/overlay.qcow2 is parsed as extra -drive options and launch fails. This is an ordinary defect in existing launch behavior, not a request to add a new requirement.","target":"c144c51fac80b5af5b01d7e8cbfa5629f7b2c264"},"finding_id":"9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568","previous_event_id":"a02f32e27e611195e41dd56c1b69b9a9b7e208b44245ba8ddbf76049e1863df9","review_id":"f1b5131645f96822be0f07c1707f2cbcab3333693f6cab11de508eb6e932b92d"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568:234cacf01cb6c25049a1c718bdba57272c2176c69549bf5b7f3d98fc10e38804"}